mink-optee-test for Debian
==========================

Overview
--------
This package provides xtest-qtee, a Qualcomm-adapted build of the upstream
OP-TEE test suite (optee_test). It targets the Qualcomm Trusted Execution
Environment (QTEE) via the MinkIPC transport stack instead of the upstream
OP-TEE supplicant daemon.

The installed binary is xtest_qtee, located in /usr/bin/.

Qualcomm-specific Adaptations
------------------------------
The following Debian patches are applied on top of the upstream optee_test
source to produce the QTEE-targeted build:

  * remove-regression-suite-from-default.patch
    Removes the upstream regression test suite from the default test suite
    string. Regression tests can still be enabled at compile time by defining
    WITH_REGRESSION_TESTS.

  * stub-testcases-inapplicable-for-qtee.patch
    Guards test cases that are not supported by QTEE (e.g. pkcs11_1016 RNG
    tests) behind a BUILD_FOR_OPTEE preprocessor flag so they are omitted
    from the QTEE build.

  * build-xtest.patch
    Replaces the upstream CMakeLists.txt with a build that links against the
    Qualcomm MinkIPC libraries (minkteec, minkadaptor) and the PKCS#11
    client (ckteec) instead of the upstream libteec / tee-supplicant.

  * rename-xtest-to-xtest-qtee.patch
    Renames the project and binary to xtest_qtee and links libckqteec
    (provided by mink-optee-client-dev).

  * find-mink-libs-via-pkgconf.patch
    Locate libminkteec and libminkadaptor via pkg-config metadata, as
    provided by mink-optee-client-dev.

Packages
--------

xtest-qtee
 The `xtest-qtee` package provides a suite of cross-platform test utilities
 designed for Qualcomm Trusted Execution Environment (QTEE) validation. It
 includes test binaries used to verify the correctness and integrity of QTEE
 components on Qualcomm-based platforms.
